  "note": "A brigade's break-in across a water obstacle (IBB S46 paras 19-23 pp 238-239, Figs 20-22). Plan metres from H (the click on the water), y across to the far bank. Two battalions up on narrow fronts of 500-800 m (650) with 500-600 m (550) between them, their start line the water line, each crossing on two places (one per assault Coy); phase 1 (PL 1) about 300-600 m ahead of the bund (450) on 1800-2000 m (1900); the third battalion passes through to about 1500 m deep (para 22, Fig 21); the bridgehead (BH) 3500-4000 m (3750) wide and 1500-1800 m (1650) deep. The follow-up bridge between the leading battalions (Fig 21), bases of fire on the home bank's flanks (Fig 20), a Bn Assy Area per assault battalion and the Bde Assy Area (IC s71 para 7 pp 362-363). With the terrain the BH line reaches out to take the ground that observes the crossing places (IBB S46 para 24 c p240), up to its doctrinal depth.",
